+{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"beec94bb-07ed-4444-9ea6-49797267a66e","agentId":"a610568719f0ad7ee","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Work in /sandbox (relative paths only for files you write). Python: /opt/robocode-strict/bin/python. A black-box gym env is reachable via `from env_client import make_env; env=make_env(); obs,info=env.reset(seed=0); obs,r,term,trunc,info=env.step(action)`. obs is an ObjectCentricState: `obs.get_objects(env.observation_space.get_type('rover'))`, `obs.get(obj,'x')`, `obj.name`. Rover features: x,y,theta,store_full,calibrated,at_home. Obstacle features x,y,z,half_x,half_y,half_z (boxes). Action is 8 floats: [dx0,dy0,dtheta0,sel0, dx1,dy1,dtheta1,sel1], dx/dy in [-0.2,0.2], dtheta in [-0.4,0.4], sel=0 is noop. Arena is 5m square (likely [-2.5,2.5]^2). Rovers start at (1,-1.75) and (-1,-1.75). There's a hidden wall down the middle of the arena (x≈0) that is NOT in the observation; from a render it appears to possibly have a gap/door somewhere. A motion that would cause collision is rejected entirely (rover stays put).\n\nDetermine empirically (write scripts, keep output short):\n1. Are dx,dy in world frame (independent of theta)? Is the motion applied exactly (position += delta) or clipped/scaled? Is theta wrapped?\n2. The exact geometry of the hidden wall: its x extent (thickness) and which y ranges are blocked, i.e. find any gap(s) where a rover can cross from x>0 to x<0. Do this for several seeds (0..5) to check it is fixed across episodes. Hint: drive rover0 to various y positions on the right side and try to step left in small increments; find the rover's min reachable x at each y (use fine y steps like 0.1 and also binary-search boundaries). Watch out for pillars (obstacles with half 0.05) and mounds (half 0.25 at y=2) blocking you; note them.\n3. The rover collision footprint: e.g. radius of a circle (or box?) — find by approaching a pillar (box half 0.05) and a wall from different directions and recording the closest reachable center distance. Also check arena boundary limits (max reachable x,y), and whether collision with other rover is checked.\n4. Does episode terminate/truncate at any point with random actions? What's the reward per step?\nReport concise numeric findings: wall geometry, rover radius/shape, arena bounds, motion semantics. Save your helper code as probe_motion.py."},"uuid":"c0de87a6-afb9-4b40-905d-5b22e17f7159","timestamp":"2026-10-01T07:23:28.283Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-cli","cwd":"/sandbox","sessionId":"2bdabd45-4dd3-4ae3-a755-e3071de60b54","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"master"}
