sible itself? does calibration get consumed?\n3. send: lander visible within 4m — test distances, heading dependence, and occlusion by pillars. Does send transmit images and analyses (received_image/received_analysis)?\n4. sample: within 0.25m of sample base; verify; drop; can a sample be sampled twice / by both rovers? Does sample object disappear or move?\n5. Is there termination when the full goal is achieved (both rovers back at start, stores empty, all received)? What does at_home require (exact position? tolerance? heading?).\nDriving: write a simple helper that moves a rover toward a target with steps clipped to 0.2, (it may get stuck on obstacles; choose easy targets on the same side of the wall, e.g. rover1 on the left side x<0, rover0 on the right side x>0). Keep printed output short. Report concise numeric findings. Save helper code as probe_vis.py."},"uuid":"a9ebd425-1f19-4ef6-8781-ae360cb6a40a","timestamp":"2026-10-01T07:23:38.716Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-cli","cwd":"/sandbox","sessionId":"2bdabd45-4dd3-4ae3-a755-e3071de60b54","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"master"}
